We are building an interactive competition flying map display using React Typescript and Tailwind/DaisyUI CSS. The application fetches information about the current navigation task from a rest interface. This contains data about the task itself as well as all previous competition data for all participants. Real time data is received through a websocket. The application should support both real time display of the flights as well as provide an option for playing back the competition at a configurable speed. There are some existing components for rendering the route and the predicted score at the next gate that can be reused. These should be ported to Typescript and placed inside the new application. The competition display map should be made available through the front end router.

The navigation task itself is available through the following API endpoint: /api/v1/contests/632/navigationtasks/2129/
It returns the following data block:
