For each contestant in the contestant we fetched the already existing track data from the endpoint: /api/v1/contests/632/navigationtasks/2129/contestants/10251/paginated_track_data
This endpoint returns a list positions for the contestant like this:
{
    "next": "cD0yMDI0LTA3LTA0KzE5JTNBNDclM0E0NiUyQjAwJTNBMDA=",
    "previous": "cj0xJnA9MjAyNC0wNy0wNCsxOSUzQTE3JTNBMTclMkIwMCUzQTAw",
    "results": [
        {
            "time": "2024-07-04T19:17:17Z",
            "latitude": 60.88434975,
            "longitude": 11.65853087,
            "speed": 82.69112553964233,
            "course": 43.400001525878906,
            "altitude": 347.817138671875,
            "progress": 0
        },
    ]
}
It is a paginated endpoint where the next page fetched by including the URL parameter cursor=data.next When fetching from the main endpoint.

In addition to the track each contestant has score data that can be F fetched from the endpoint: /api/v1/contests/632/navigationtasks/2129/contestants/10251/score_data/
It contains a list of all the scoring events for the contestant. There are several types of events, like passing away point Comm missing away point, backtracking, flying outside the corridor, etc.
