Real time data is Received through a websocket connection to the endpoint: /ws/tracks/2129/
This continuously receives real time tracking data and scoring data from all competing aircraft. There are kinds of data blocks. The exact data blocks can be inferred by studying navigationTask.js. This also contains some information about how the routes are rendered. It also contains all logic old version of this application.


The components that can be reused are:
the files in danger_thermometer: which displays A thermometer which indicates the danger level relative to the corridor edge or danger zones in the area
the renderers inside trackRenderers: These these components know how to render the different track types like Precision Air navigation Race Air sports race air sports challenge.
teamBadges.js Is used to display information about the competing team and their current score in the lower right hand corner of the map
gateScoreArrow: It displays the predicted score at the next gate crossing with a nice animated arrow that moves up and down a point scale.

Create this new feature in the react_vite folder. We should have a map that This place each contestant as an airplane icon with correct orientation according to course. Each icon should have a trail that covers the past few minutes of flight. It should be possible to toggle on and off the full trail for all flights. The page should have results table that shows the current core and standing of the contestants.

Do not use axios or any other non-standard libraries even if this is used in the old solution. Try to use standardized tools. 

When in doubt do what is done in reactjs, but better.